; Prusa MK4S acoustic speed sweep
; generated by: ./gen_noise_sweep.py --phase-ab --out gcode/mk4s_ab_phase.gcode
;
; segments        : 18
; est. runtime    : 3:47 (mm:ss; junction deviation ignored, runs a touch short)
; measured time   : 2:10 across all windows
; acceleration    : 4000 mm/s^2 (M201+M204; 1250 is only the startup value, HWLIMIT allows 7000)
; junction dev.   : 0.01 mm
; measure / pause : 5 / 2 s
; glide           : 30 s per axis
; feature check   : M862.6 Input shaper
; phase stepping  : ON (M970)
; per-axis ceiling: 300 mm/s, firmware HWLIMIT_NORMAL_MAX_FEEDRATE
; Z parked at     : 50 mm
; X/Y motors      : 200-step, 16 microsteps, stock current X300 Y370 mA
; full-step rate  : 6.25 Hz per mm/s (electrical 1.5625 Hz per mm/s)
;
; WHICH HARMONIC IS LOUDEST TELLS YOU WHAT IS WRONG.  Per segment the CSV
; gives elec_hz; one electrical cycle is four full steps, so:
;   4x elec_hz  = the full-step rate: cogging.  Always present, always normal.
;   2x elec_hz  = phase amplitude imbalance - one coil pulling weaker than
;                 the other.  Bad crimp, partly seated connector, damaged
;                 winding, or a driver channel down.
;   1x elec_hz  = DC offset in one phase.
; Normal singing peaks at 4x.  A peak at 2x louder than the one at 4x is a
; fault signature, and no amount of current or damping will fix it.
;
; Cold run: heaters stay off so the hotend fan never starts and the meter
; only hears the motion system.  Each axis runs end to end at every speed,
; so nothing repositions between segments.  One beep = the next window
; starts in 2 s; three beeps = end of file.
;
; ON-SCREEN SPEED: every move is commanded F6000 (100 mm/s) and M220 carries
; the real speed, so the printer's speed field reads mm/s directly - 240%
; means 240 mm/s.  Sanity check on the first run: the segments must audibly
; differ.  If they all sound the same the firmware is ignoring M220 on travel
; moves - regenerate with --speed-display off and read the CSV instead.
;
; cold noise sweep - no heaters, no extrusion, nothing gets printed
; the same print checks PrusaSlicer 2.9.6 emits for this printer. Without the
; feature check the printer warns the file is not sliced for input shaping and
; runs it down a legacy compatibility path - different limits, different noise.
M862.3 P "MK4S"
M862.5 P2
M862.6 P"Input shaper"
M104 S0
M140 S0
M107
G21
G90
M220 S100

; --- home and park (noisy, not measured) ---
M17
G28
G1 X125.000 Y105.000 Z50.000 F1800  ; park

; --- phase stepping ON ---
; set explicitly, after homing. On an MK4 the enable flag defaults to FALSE
; (defaults.hpp: true only for XL/CoreOne/iX) and is declared ram_only, so it
; reverts to OFF at every power cycle. PrusaSlicer never sends M970, so a print
; runs without phase stepping unless something enables it after boot.
; M972 saves the correction table but does NOT enable - separate states.
M970 X1 Y1
G4 P1000  ; let the drivers switch over

; --- motion limits, held constant for the whole run ---
; planner starts at M201 X1250 Y1250; raising to 4000 (HWLIMIT_NORMAL_MAX_ACCELERATION allows 7000)
; PrusaSlicer emits M203 X300 Y300 for this printer too - the 400 in the
; firmware header is a startup value the HWLIMIT never lets you reach.
; NOTE: a PrusaSlicer print ENDS with M593 X T2 F0 / M593 Y T2 F0, which turns
; input shaping off and leaves it off until reboot. Power-cycle the printer
; before measuring, or this file may run with a different shaper state.
; M203 is set to the hard limit, not the 400 startup value: HWLIMIT clamps X/Y to 300 mm/s and asking for more is a no-op
M201 X4000 Y4000 Z200 E2500  ; maximum accelerations, mm/s^2
M203 X300 Y300 Z40 E100  ; maximum feedrates, mm/s
M204 P4000 R2500 T4000  ; acceleration, mm/s^2
M205 X8.00 Y8.00 Z2.00 E10.00  ; jerk limits, mm/s
M205 J0.010  ; junction deviation, mm
M205 S0 T0  ; minimum extruding and travel feed rate, mm/s

; --- BASELINE (start): motors energised, nothing moving ---
M400
G4 P2000  ; silence
M117 baseline start
M300 S1200 P60
G4 P10000  ; hold still

; ====================================================================
; X phase stepping A/B
; ====================================================================
G1 X5.000 F6000  ; to X end

; -- X @ 30 mm/s, phase stepping off --
M400
M970 X0
G4 P2000  ; let the driver settle
M220 S30
M117 X 30 phase stepping off
M300 S600 P60
G1 X35.000 F6000
M117 X 30 phase stepping off
G1 X65.000 F6000
M117 X 30 phase stepping off
